WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.608
More than three thousand years ago, the people of Shang created an early form of writing.

00:00:04.958 --> 00:00:09.566
They carved the characters onto turtle shells and animal bones.

00:00:09.916 --> 00:00:13.156
When people faced important matters, they would come to ask the spirits.

00:00:13.506 --> 00:00:17.538
They heated the turtle shells and read the cracks to guess the answers.

00:00:17.888 --> 00:00:22.832
The priest carved the questions and results down, stroke by stroke.

00:00:23.182 --> 00:00:27.310
These ancient characters are called oracle-bone script.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:31.956
Oracle-bone script recorded rituals and matters of everyday life.

00:00:32.306 --> 00:00:35.954
The royal house carefully preserved the bones.

00:00:36.304 --> 00:00:40.336
Thousands of years passed, and the oracle bones lay buried in the earth.

00:00:40.686 --> 00:00:44.406
Only in modern times did people rediscover them.

00:00:44.756 --> 00:00:48.788
Many of today's Chinese characters evolved from oracle-bone script.

00:00:49.138 --> 00:00:54.778
Looking at sun, moon, mountain and water, we can still find the wisdom of the ancients.

